# TICKET: Links Lost During HTML-to-Markdown Body Conversion

## Priority: Medium
## Component: packages/tomd (HTML body converter)
## Discovered: 2026-04-29 via manual audit of n5034.html vs n5034.md

---

## Problem

When tomd converts HTML papers to Markdown, hyperlinks (`<a href="...">`) are lost in two specific scenarios:

1. **Tables nested inside list items (`<li>`)**: The table-flattening logic strips the `<a>` tags and keeps only the inner text.
2. **Links inside headings (`<h2>`)**: When an `<a>` tag is embedded in a heading element, the link URL is dropped; only the text survives.

This is a **data loss bug** in the body converter. The YAML frontmatter/metadata extraction is unaffected and working correctly.

