---

## Root Cause Analysis

The HTML body converter in tomd has two related issues:

### Issue 1: Table-in-List Flattening

The HTML structure for the Editor's reports section is:

```html
<li>Editor's reports, approval/adoption of working drafts
  <table border="1">
    <thead><tr><th>Document</th><th>Editor's report</th><th>Prospective WD</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr>
      <td>C++ 26 Working Draft</td>
      <td><a href="https://wg21.link/N5032">N5032</a></td>
      <td><a href="https://wg21.link/N5033">N5033</a></td>
    </tr></tbody>
  </table>
</li>
```

The converter flattens this into a single line of text:
```
Editor's reports, approval/adoption of working drafts Document Editor's report Prospective WD C++ 26 Working Draft N5032 N5033
```

The `<a>` tags inside `<td>` cells are stripped to bare text during flattening.

### Issue 2: Links Inside Headings

```html
<h2>Meeting notice and location:
  <a href="https://isocpp.org/files/papers/N5024.pdf">N5024</a>
</h2>
```

Becomes:
```markdown
## Meeting notice and location: N5024
```

The `<a>` tag inside the `<h2>` is reduced to its text content; the href is lost.

